Review this incremental model. `models/marts/fct_page_views.sql`:
```sql
{{ config(materialized='incremental') }}
select event_id, user_id, url, event_at
from {{ source('raw', 'page_views') }}
{% if is_incremental() %}
where event_at > (select max(event_at) from {{ this }})
{% endif %}
```
Events arrive from a Kafka topic via a CDC connector and the job runs hourly.

Review this model. `models/marts/fct_hourly_active_users.sql`:
```sql
{{ config(materialized='incremental', unique_key='user_id_hour') }}
select user_id, date_trunc('hour', current_timestamp) as event_hour,   -- windowed by when the job runs, not event time
       count(*) as event_count
from {{ source('raw', 'app_events') }}
{% if is_incremental() %}
where _loaded_at > (select coalesce(max(event_hour), '1970-01-01') from {{ this }})
{% endif %}
group by 1, 2
```
Events arrive via a webhook with typical delivery lag of a few minutes to a few hours; `unique_key` is correctly set and the merge strategy is `merge`.

Review this model. `models/marts/fct_subscription_events.sql`:
```sql
{{ config(materialized='incremental') }}
-- idempotent: safe to re-run any window without side effects
select subscription_id, event_type, event_at
from {{ source('raw', 'subscription_events') }}
{% if is_incremental() %}
where event_at > (select max(event_at) from {{ this }})
{% endif %}
```
No `unique_key` is configured.

Review this model. `models/marts/fct_hourly_active_users.sql`:
```sql
{{ config(materialized='incremental', unique_key='user_id_hour') }}
select user_id, date_trunc('hour', event_at) as event_hour,   -- windowed by the event's own timestamp
       count(*) as event_count
from {{ source('raw', 'app_events') }}
{% if is_incremental() %}
where event_at > (select max(event_hour) - interval '6 hours' from {{ this }})   -- lookback covers typical webhook lag
{% endif %}
group by 1, 2
```
